        "header": "3Methodology",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.07609/2610.07609v3/fig1_arch_tikz.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of PhysLDM.The framework consists of three main components:\n(1) ASpatial VAE(top left) that encodes the per-frame canonical mesh into a compact set of resolution-independent latent tokens.\n(2) AnST-VAE(bottom) that compresses the temporal trajectory into a single joint latent𝐙\\mathbf{Z}, which serves as the training target of the LDM.\n(3) AnLDM(top right) that predicts the entire latent trajectory from the initial state in a single diffusion pass.Dec∗\\astdenotes the frozen decoders, which decode the latent into the final full trajectory.",
                "position": 434
            }
        ]
