                "caption": "Figure 16:Beyond material estimation: designing a more informative throw.(a) Ground-truth replays of the initial and optimized release velocities atE⋆=60E^{\\star}=60kPa. Orange and blue overlays represent stiffness perturbations of−0.05-0.05and+0.05+0.05dex. The first three columns show true motion at matched times and a shared camera scale. In the final column, rigid translation and rotation offsets from the nominal trajectory are magnified by5×5\\times, using equal magnification in both rows.\n(b) Cumulative rigid-pose sensitivity, normalized by the initial throw’s final score, increases by13.4×13.4\\times. This score is computed from the unamplified GT trajectories.\n(c) Material estimation from the same distant initial guess,E0=1,000E_{0}=1{,}000kPa. After 60 estimation steps, the initial throw remains near901901kPa, whereas the optimized throw reaches73.773.7kPa, much closer to the true6060kPa. Throw design uses 30 Adam steps and approximately 7 minutes.",
